      "created_at": "2026-10-04T04:22:39Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-04T04:22:39Z",
      "body": "The missing-text-node behavior reported here for self-closing elements with attributes is fixed by commit 31bbc99adedcada7d52bc4745273e7d8b9824b31, which is included in v5.7.3 and later tags.\n\nI checked current master (80e88a8, package version 5.11.2) with the original workbookPr example plus empty paired tags, boolean attributes, and custom textNodeName, with alwaysCreateTextNode both enabled and disabled: all 16 checks pass. With the option enabled, the attributed self-closing element includes an empty text property; with it disabled, the existing attribute-only output is preserved.\n\nThis addresses the missing #text report, but does not add the separate option requested in the opening post to exclude text nodes specifically for self-closing elements.\r\n",
